{
  // Client/Vitest tests. Extends the CLIENT config for its narrower `include`.
  //
  // It does NOT differ from the node config on `lib`: the root config already
  // sets `["ES2022","DOM","DOM.Iterable"]` and `tsconfig.client.json` adds no
  // `compilerOptions` at all, so the two resolved option sets are identical
  // apart from `allowJs`. Do not write a comment here claiming this config is
  // what puts DOM in scope -- an earlier version did, describing a protection
  // that cannot fire, because there is no configuration under which the node
  // program lacks DOM.
  //
  // What the overlap on `tests/helpers` actually buys is the `*.svelte.ts`
  // split: those rune cells are excluded from the node config and owned here,
  // because only this program pulls in Svelte's ambient `$state`.
  //
  // KNOWN GAP, stated rather than papered over: bare `tsc` resolves
  // `import ... from "./Foo.svelte"` through an ambient module declaration and
  // never reads the component's own <script> block. The three harness
  // components under `tests/client/fixtures/` are therefore NOT typechecked by
  // this config. Only `svelte-check` would cover them, and it is scoped to
  // `src/client` today. Do not describe this config as covering them.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.client.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": [
    "src/client/**/*.ts",
    "src/shared/**/*.ts",
    // Express 5 ships no usable types, so `src/server/express.d.ts` is a
    // hand-written `declare module "express"`. An ambient declaration only
    // applies to programs that INCLUDE the file declaring it -- and client
    // tests reach server route modules transitively, which then lose the
    // declaration and report `express` as implicitly `any` (TS7016) in ~29
    // files that are not what these tests are about. Included by path rather
    // than by pulling in all of `src/server`.
    "src/server/express.d.ts",
    "tests/client/**/*.ts",
    "tests/design-system-impl/**/*.ts",
    "tests/helpers/**/*.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"]
}
